  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM &#x2013; Multi Country Humanitarian Assistance &#x2013; CAP 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to Round 11 of IOM&#x2019;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) monitoring of displacement and return movement, 2,017,236 people remain displaced in South Sudan, 78 per cent of which are sheltering with already crisis-affected host communities. Displacement figures have continued to increase despite the signing of the Revitalised Agreement on the Resolution of the Conflict in the Republic of South Sudan (R-ARCSS) in 2018 due to an increase of displacement-inducing incidents such as sub-national conflict and unprecedented climate-related disasters. This project intends to ensure that the displaced communities living in the Bentiu, Naivasha, and Hai Masna displacement sites have continued, unhindered and equitable access to humanitarian services and assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
